WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.468
-Welcome back.
We're here with Dan Levy.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.936
And we are about to play a
brand-new game called

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:06.940
"Best, Worst, First."

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.174
-♪ Best ♪

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.509
♪ Worst ♪

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.277
♪ First ♪

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.344
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:13.446
I'll hit this button here,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.682
which activates
a random topic generator.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.883
It will land
on a random prompt,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.751
like "Best pick-up line
you have ever used"

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.987
or "Worst lie you
ever have told."

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.255
Whatever it lands on,
you have to tell the first story

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.191
or memory that comes to
our minds.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.593
Are you ready for this?
-Okay. Yeah, I'm ready.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:30.163
-Alright, first up is "Best."

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:35.468 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.303 line:0%
Best late-night snack.
Alright, I got one.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.671 line:0%
-Ooh!
-Dan, what is yours?

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.140 line:0%
-Okay. I have recently
been doing --

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.177 line:0%
I can only do a savory and
a sweet together.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:48.114 line:0%
So I have been doing gummies
that I put in the refrigerator,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.949 line:0%
because I like them
cold and chewy,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.151 line:0%
and then I do a popcorn.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:56.155 line:0%
And, recently, my friend got me
onto nutritional yeast,

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.491 line:0%
so I have been doing, like, a
nutritional-yeast popcorn.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.561 line:0%
And I was eating
my gummies and popcorn,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.162 line:0%
and it was kind of,
I would imagine,

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.031 line:0%
lit only by the refrigerator,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.534 line:0%
looked like a
really intense late-night binge.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.936 line:0%
And then I looked out my window,

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.806 line:0%
and there was someone
just really concerned

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.507 line:0%
staring back at me
from the apartment

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:19.245 line:0%
just across the way, so if you
are going to late-night-snack,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.546 line:0%
maybe lower the blinds,

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.916 line:0%
unless you want
to just entertain people,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.917 line:0%
or, in her case, I think she was

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.219 line:0%
looking at me like,
"Poor thing."

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.222 line:0%
-My late-night snack is --
What I do is,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.491 line:0%
if I ever get pizza, I order
pizza, I order two pies.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:35.361 line:0%
The second pie,
I take out individual slices,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.429 line:0%
put them in Ziploc bags,
and freeze them.

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.898 line:0%
And then, when I feel like
a late-night snack,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.300 line:0%
I throw it in the toaster oven.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.969 line:0%
And I know how to
zhuzh it up perfect,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.138 line:0%
and it tastes like
a fresh slice.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:50.576 line:0%
-Hot tips.
-Welcome back to "Hot Tips."

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:51.711 line:0%
Okay, here we go.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.479 line:0%
Next round,
it's time for the worst.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.248 line:0%
Here we go. Worst!
-Alright.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:58.617 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:03.623 line:0%
Okay. Worst fear. Dan.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.459 line:0%
-I'll just --
I have no shame about this.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:10.329 line:0%
My worst fear is
moths and butterflies,

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.465 line:0%
which is a strange --
It's a strange fear to have.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.534 line:0%
-That's the worst fear
of all of the fears?

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.934 line:0%
-Listen, I'm owning it.

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:19.571 line:0%
They have powdery,
very weird wings

00:02:19.571 --> 00:02:22.275 line:0%
and they don't fly
in any particular direction.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.911 line:0%
And that -- Yeah, it's that.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.912 line:0%
It's the frantic
kind of flapping.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.347 line:0%
-Yes, it's the flapping.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.850 line:0%
-Inevitably, I think they're
going to end up in my mouth.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.652 line:0%
I can't rationalize
this fear, Jimmy.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.753 line:0%
-Wow.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.788 line:0%
-All I can do is
share it with you tonight.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.857 line:0%
-Last round,
it's time for "First."

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.026 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.296 line:0%
First concert?
First...acting credit.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:46.632 line:0%
That's interesting.
Dan, first acting credit.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:55.008 line:0%
-My first big opportunity was
playing a murderous tech person

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:59.812 line:0%
in a Lifetime film where I was
out to murder Mischa Barton.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.681 line:0%
-What?!
-And -- Yeah.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.982 line:0%
And the fun plot twist
is that we realized

00:03:03.982 --> 00:03:08.354 line:0%
that I actually had
also murdered her parents.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.623 line:0%
But anyone who watches
this Lifetime movie,

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.891 line:0%
if they were to actually put
the pieces together,

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:15.428 line:0%
would realize that,
in terms of the timeline

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.330 line:0%
of this character's life,
I had to have

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.333 line:0%
murdered her parents when I was
about 10 1/2 years old.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:25.070 line:0%
So I don't want to say that
this movie is a masterpiece

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.206 line:0%
or anything,
but it's certainly something

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:32.645 line:0%
that shaped my career in really
pivotal and fundamental ways.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.247 line:0%
-I feel like we get
Blumhouse on this

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:37.316 line:0%
and remake this into
a giant feature film.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.552 line:0%
I'm into it.
-It would be a tough pitch.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.387 line:0%
-First acting credit, weirdly,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.656 line:0%
because, tonight, we also have
the great Michael J. Fox

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.358 line:0%
on the show,
his show "Spin City."

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.327 line:0%
-Canadian legend.
-He is a Canadian legend.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.362 line:0%
-Mm-hmm.
-"Spin City."

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.164 line:0%
I was on an episode of
"Spin City."

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:54.767 line:0%
I auditioned in New York City.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.436 line:0%
And I played
a photographer that, like,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.470 line:0%
took a Polaroid picture
of, like --

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.340 line:0%
And I was so excited for
the audition,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.210 line:0%
I went in and
I had this weird jacket

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.112 line:0%
that I got at
a store called Structure

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.146 line:0%
that doesn't exist anymore.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.247 line:0%
I don't know if you
remember that.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.116 line:0%
And I had this jacket on
and this sweater,

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.250 line:0%
and I went in
and I got the audition.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.618 line:0%
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:13.753 line:0%
I go, "When do I go in for
wardrobe or who do I meet?"

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.288 line:0%
Blah, blah, blah.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:18.924 line:0%
And they go, "Just wear exactly
what you wore in the audition."

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.326 line:0%
Dude, I'm going to
find that movie,

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.861 line:0%
and we got to talk more about
that when you come back.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.162 line:0%
-Please don't.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:26.298 line:0%
-I'm psyched about your new
movie, "Happiest Season,"

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:29.068 line:0%
is available on Hulu
November 25th.

